{"title":"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangle has vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/2249ef41e3aabf1d1e65de53e8c1fd4f76759a6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6m,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8cab3b86d4a13c3cc3680c32aaa80cc854689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> divides the triangle into two triangles of equal area. What is the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a928b43ca7d1b13cdcac3ba059580bdf0c9be9d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{A} - \\!\\frac {1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} - \\!\\frac {1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac {1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac {1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"383\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's label the three points as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56c2d75970eccaf7b305f042636bcebdb2a1cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a614885d3185761a5744a0de9ebd12a58201426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f30549ba35b32cf668596dc204dc001ee23e80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(6m,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Clearly, whenever the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1fe0afdea68630af2bda225ce5f2978b5ba0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> intersects the inside of the triangle, it will intersect the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of intersection. \n</p><p>The triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> have the same height, which is the distance between the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\nHence they have equal areas if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The midpoint of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591e74d0bac255900624ff32a05708e6d4194830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac{6m+1}2, \\frac 12 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"104\" height=\"43\" />. This point lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1fe0afdea68630af2bda225ce5f2978b5ba0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c2a0324042d2ffee44a4a1b4bf6c1159ab9f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 = m \\cdot \\frac{6m+1}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"125\" height=\"37\" />. This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/844c79c8ec1d9cdba8e416fbf615a8e9b5ffb91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m^2 + m - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />. Using Vieta's formulas, we find that the sum of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/1959e8791326371c179908c681dfc6bb26ccd4db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} - \\!\\frac {1}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"72\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor illustration, below are pictures of the situation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a499235a34b7f1551248489c227099d9936aff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a56cd0d239005a50cc947396700c6f0e3acd75f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=0.5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1bb8db193a3415ae209659079707b418c9c740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/70674cda448c1bb51efbedaeec565c0d9000bdc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=-1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee0289fb1f74e7bf8b303d3db34f731e6f637d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(0.8); real m=1.5; draw( (0,0)--(1,1)--(6*m,0)--cycle ); draw( ((-0.5)*(1,m)) -- ((1.5)*(1,m)), dashed ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,1),NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(6*m,0),E); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920597b66dc7afdf08e499aa29a879582a966bfd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(0.8); real m=0.5; draw( (0,0)--(1,1)--(6*m,0)--cycle ); draw( ((-1)*(1,m)) -- (3*(1,m)), dashed ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,1),N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(6*m,0),E); pair D = intersectionpoint( (1,1)--(6*m,0), ((-1)*(1,m)) -- (3*(1,m)) ); dot(D); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); [/asy]\" width=\"405\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28bd630603b59402c8d7a30b20ac1fa955b987a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(0.8); real m=1/3; draw( (0,0)--(1,1)--(6*m,0)--cycle ); draw( ((-1)*(1,m)) -- (3*(1,m)), dashed ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,1),N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(6*m,0),E); pair D = intersectionpoint( (1,1)--(6*m,0), ((-1)*(1,m)) -- (3*(1,m)) ); dot(D); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); [/asy]\" width=\"382\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a90b71d893fb87d66d3bab05651a8ecfd69317a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(0.8); real m=-1/2; draw( (0,0)--(1,1)--(6*m,0)--cycle ); draw( ((-2)*(1,m)) -- (1*(1,m)), dashed ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,1),NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(6*m,0),W); pair D = intersectionpoint( (1,1)--(6*m,0), ((-1)*(1,m)) -- (3*(1,m)) ); dot(D); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); [/asy]\" width=\"425\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p>Note&#160;: In contests when you get problems like these, your AOPS knowledge will not be enough. AOPs books are just the basic, always prep for more.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line must pass through the triangle's centroid, since the line divides the triangle in half. The coordinates of the centroid are found by averaging those of the vertices. The slope of the line from the origin through the centroid is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b436b59d8d15978dfde0a7739f7b1c2b3bc942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{1+6m}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"45\" height=\"49\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb0c8b06def7670778e70b6215560b8039ec6cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{1+6m}{3}}=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"83\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d6c311738a8150f6574a05d46221371cb831a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}=m\\left(\\frac{1+6m}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"139\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b90768a98de11b52b630adca61b25654e78dd1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=m(1+6m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e238e395c37202c0a30e764bd2ee7a784ac5882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6m^2+m-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Using Vieta's Formulas, the sum of the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25bbcae7adb42d6352e9b035cb9ef226a31c5829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\; -\\frac{1}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"80\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A\">2009 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n